+### D-146 · 2026-08-30 · Pre-execution audit stops the authorised launch and closes five production evidence gaps before data
+
+**Audit stop, before any preflight or fit:** two independent read-only passes were run after D-145 rather than treating implementation tests as launch authority. They found: (1) mounted batch sync copied journals directly to final paths and did not fsync files/directories; (2) a Windows-spawned fit was not bound to the preflight commit, so a clean mid-batch commit could mix source revisions; (3) time-only stale-lease recovery could seize a live long-running owner; (4) the repair-label helper ran all 60 fits in-process without lease/timeout/staging/sync and automatically opened the exclusion-rate comparison that D-144 places in Week 8; and (5) Experiment 1 had no immediate launch-start receipt or validated partial monitor. The owner-authorised execution was stopped with all confirmatory roots empty. One long synthetic pytest worker was interrupted and inspected; it had invoked no unmocked fit boundary.
+
+**Fixes before execution:** mounted sync now stages on the destination filesystem, fsyncs bytes, atomically publishes, syncs directory metadata where supported and independently reads back before acknowledgement. The exact preflight commit travels in the spawned payload, is checked before pool generation and again while loading every sidecar. Any non-`None` stale-age request now refuses before filesystem access; only token-authorised release exists until heartbeat/liveness evidence can be implemented. The old public repair-label entry refuses before access. A dedicated no-compute smoke preflight and fixed launcher own the exact unit `d5baeb907ac3`, seeds 1000–1019 and baseline/data/feature order; every one of 60 sidecars runs in a fresh timed process with same-volume staging, immutable publication, lease, exact-commit reload and independent incremental sync. Its final artifact is label plus four counts only—no exclusion total/rate, 0.00 comparison, shortfall or reserve action. Experiment 1 now writes matching local/durable launch-start evidence before its blocking batch call, and the read-only monitor validates the exact manifest, event transitions, fit evidence, sync receipts, remote trees, common commit and progress counts without calculating H1.
+
+**Verification/data:** durable-sync/commit-binding focused matrix **233 passed, 1 skipped**; launch/monitor/lease matrix **113 passed, 1 skipped**; complete repair-label evidence/smoke matrix **82 passed, 1 skipped in 541.86 s**. Each skip is the Windows unprivileged-symlink case with non-link companions. These matrices overlap and are not added as a test total. The final D-146 repository-wide gate then passed **1,659 tests, skipped 7 and failed 0 in 1,213.80 s**; skips were three CUDA-device checks, three Windows unprivileged-symlink cases and one intentionally vacuous identity case. The verified implementation is local handoff commit `7a8960d`; the clean package state remains reconstructed history, never remote ancestry. Four fresh Experiment-1 roots and four separate smoke roots were created and rechecked empty; separating them prevents either preflight canary namespace from overwriting the other. **No preflight, confirmatory dataset, fit, label, result, GPU work, reserve action or scientific statistic exists.** The frozen CPU one-hour timeout remains. **Plan ref:** S§W6 Mon–Sun; D-033, D-034, D-096, D-140…D-145; DEV-011, DEV-017. **Reviewed by Sol:** not yet — delta 67.
